---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import JourneyMap from "../components/JourneyMap.astro";
import AreasAccessMap from "../components/AreasAccessMap.astro";

const otherAreas = [
  {
    slug: "puncak-nipah",
    name: "Puncak Nipah",
    text: `From <strong>Nipah</strong> beach. The single-pitch sport wall is reached on a
      levelled path along its base; the approach to the summit tower (the Green Line Route) is
      not well described in the source.`,
    unclear: true,
  },
  {
    slug: "mumbar-cliff",
    name: "Mumbar Cliff",
    text: `From the <strong>Nipah</strong> side: the Nipah–Tunamaya coastal concrete path, down
      to the beach, then up the dry riverbed following cairns ~20–30 min to yellow blazes on the
      trees, then a cut jungle trail 30–40 min to the wall. About 2 h 20 on foot, or a boat to
      Tunamaya / the beach + ~1 h 20. The <strong>west side of the cliff needs a new approach
      path</strong>.`,
    unclear: false,
  },
  {
    slug: "bagus-tower",
    name: "Bagus Tower",
    text: `Follow the road to <strong>Bagus Place</strong> to its end, then up into the jungle,
      about 1 h. The trail was cut in October 2015 — <strong>expect heavy regrowth</strong>; bring
      a machete.`,
    unclear: true,
  },
  {
    slug: "batu-sirau",
    name: "Batu Sirau (Mystery Pinnacle)",
    text: `Behind Gunung Nenek Semukut, on a summit access path from the Nenek Semukut side. A
      possible newer approach "from the river landslide" is noted in the source but
      <strong>unexplored</strong>.`,
    unclear: true,
  },
  {
    slug: "juara-beach",
    name: "Juara Beach",
    text: `East coast — reached by the cross-island road/trail from Tekek, or by boat. The
      climbing here is <strong>undocumented</strong> beyond a single field sketch.`,
    unclear: true,
  },
];

const steps = [
  {
    title: "Get to Mersing",
    body: `<strong>Mersing</strong> (Johor) is the main ferry port for Tioman;
      <strong>Tanjung Gemok</strong> (Endau, Pahang) is an alternative a little to the north.
      From Kuala Lumpur it's roughly a 4–5&nbsp;h drive or bus; from Singapore about 3–4&nbsp;h
      via the Second Link. Nearest airports are Senai (Johor Bahru) or Kuala Lumpur, then a bus
      or transfer to the jetty. Aim to arrive the night before an early ferry.`,
  },
  {
    title: "Ferry to Mukut — direct is the main way",
    body: `There is usually a <strong>ferry direct from Mersing to Kampung Mukut</strong>, though
      it runs at <strong>lower frequency</strong> than the west-coast sailings. This is the
      simplest way in — build your dates around it.
      <br><br>
      <strong>Alternative:</strong> take a ferry to <strong>Genting</strong> (the southernmost
      west-coast village), then a short <strong>boat</strong> round the south of the island to
      Mukut.
      <br><br>
      Either way, <strong>check the schedule before you book travel</strong> — sailings are
      tide-dependent and the timetable is usually only published about a
      <strong>month in advance</strong>; crossings are cancelled in rough weather, and the
      north-east monsoon (Nov–Feb) disrupts them badly.`,
  },
  {
    title: "Arrange the boat in advance",
    body: `If you need a <strong>sea taxi or charter boat</strong> — for the Genting–Mukut hop,
      or to reach Mumbar and the Nipah-side crags — <strong>set it up well before you arrive</strong>.
      Ask your <strong>homestay owner</strong> to help organise it with a local boatman; don't
      count on sorting a boat on the day.`,
  },
  {
    title: "Find a place to stay in Mukut",
    body: `Mukut is a small fishing village. Options are the <strong>Simukut Hillview</strong>
      lodge and <strong>homestays run by local families</strong> — arrange through
      <strong>Tam Haja</strong> or &ldquo;Uncle Sam&rdquo;. Facilities are basic; bring what you
      need for the climbing. <em>More lodging detail will be added here.</em>`,
  },
  {
    title: "The jungle approach — stash a day before",
    body: `The walk-in from Mukut to the walls is steep primary jungle: <strong>1 to 2+ hours</strong>,
      and finding the exact start of a route is often the real crux. Several logbook parties
      <strong>carry their gear up and stash it near the base the day before</strong>, so their
      summit-day packs are light. Tell Tam (or your lodge) your route and expected return time
      every time you go up.`,
  },
  {
    title: "Follow the checkpoints to your route",
    body: `The Nenek Semukut trail is marked with numbered checkpoints
      (<strong>CP1 → CP9</strong>). Every approach in this guidebook is described against them:
      <strong>CP5</strong> branches to Batu Naga and Damai Sentosa; <strong>CP7</strong> to
      Polish Princess, Sam Sam, Naga, Freebird and Puncak Anak; <strong>CP9</strong> is on the
      far side of the peak. Checkpoint numbering and trail markings change over time — confirm
      the current sequence against a recent trip report or the
      <a href="https://github.com/therizhao/tioman-climbing/blob/main/dragonhorns-climb-log.pdf">route book</a>
      before you commit.`,
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Plan a trip"
  description="Step by step to the Dragon's Horns: Mersing, the Tioman ferry, Kampung Mukut, where to stay, the jungle approach and the trail checkpoints."
  section="/plan"
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/#areas">Guidebook</a><span>/</span><span>Plan a trip</span>
    </nav>

    <div class="detail-hero" style="border-bottom:0">
      <p class="label">Plan a trip</p>
      <h1>Getting to the Dragon's Horns</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Mukut has no airport and no road. Getting there is mainland → Mersing → ferry (direct,
        or via Genting) → Mukut → jungle. Here's the sequence.
      </p>
    </div>

    <JourneyMap />

    <div
      class="callout"
      style="border-color:var(--oxide);border-left-color:var(--oxide);background:var(--oxide-soft)"
    >
      <h4 style="color:var(--oxide)">Emergency contact</h4>
      <p>
        Local contact <strong>Tam Haja</strong> — <a href="tel:+60129190785"
          >+60&nbsp;12-919&nbsp;0785</a
        >, <a href="mailto:khairudinhaja@gmail.com">khairudinhaja@gmail.com</a>. Save it before you
        lose signal, and read the <a href="/emergency">emergency &amp; rescue page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="journey">
      {
        steps.map((s, i) => (
          <li class="journey-step">
            <span class="journey-n">{i + 1}</span>
            <div>
              <h2>{s.title}</h2>
              <p set:html={s.body} />
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>

    <section style="padding-top:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem)">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2 style="font-size:var(--step-2)">Getting to the other areas</h2>
        <p>
          The steps above are for the Dragon's Horns. The rest of the island's rock is scattered
          along the south-west coast and reached separately — mostly from the Nipah side.
        </p>
      </div>

      <AreasAccessMap />

      <div class="otherlist">
        {
          otherAreas.map((a) => (
            <div class="otheritem">
              <a href={`/areas/${a.slug}`}>{a.name}</a>
              <p set:html={a.text} />
              {a.unclear && (
                <p class="otherflag">
                  Access details here are thin or unverified — <strong>contributions welcome</strong>.
                  <a href="/contribute"> Add what you know →</a>
                </p>
              )}
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </section>

    <section style="padding-top:0">
      <div class="sec-head"><h2 style="font-size:var(--step-2)">Good to know</h2></div>
      <div class="two-col">
        <div style="display:grid;gap:1.25rem">
          <div class="panel">
            <span class="label">Season</span>
            <h3>When to go</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>March–April</strong> and <strong>August</strong> are the settled windows</li>
              <li>South faces bake after 1&nbsp;pm — start before dawn</li>
              <li>The steepest routes need <strong>two dry days</strong> to come into condition</li>
              <li>
                Monsoon roughly <strong>November–February</strong>: heavy rain, rough seas, ferries
                can stop
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="panel">
            <span class="label">Not a climber?</span>
            <h3>The via ferrata</h3>
            <p>
              The <a href="/areas/north-tower/via-ferrata">North Tower via ferrata</a> reaches a
              viewpoint on fixed cable and rungs — no rope skills, but still exposed. Go with a
              local guide.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <span class="label">Style &amp; safety</span>
          <h3>What to expect on the walls</h3>
          <p>
            Long runouts, some loose rock, mixed bolted and natural protection, jungle pitches to
            the summit, and committing abseil descents frequently finished in the dark.
          </p>
          <p>
            Anchors are being re-equipped over time, but older routes may still be "one bolt plus
            old tat". Helmets. Careful rope management. Loose rock has put climbers in hospital
            here.
          </p>
          <p>
            Know the <a href="/emergency">emergency &amp; rescue plan</a> before you go up, and
            carry a way to call for help — phone coverage on the walls is unreliable.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div style="height:clamp(2rem,5vw,4rem)"></div>
</Base>

<style>
  .journey {
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: none;
    margin: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .journey-step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3.5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem) 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .journey-step {
      grid-template-columns: 2.5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 1rem;
    }
  }
  .journey-n {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--oxide);
    line-height: 1;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .journey-step h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-weight: 400;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
  .journey-step p {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 0.96rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: var(--read);
  }

  .otherlist {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
  }
  .otheritem {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
  }
  .otheritem > a {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .otheritem > a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .otheritem p {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 0.94rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: var(--read);
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }
  .otherflag {
    font-size: 0.85rem !important;
    color: var(--mid) !important;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--faint);
    padding-left: 0.85rem;
  }
  .otherflag strong {
    color: var(--oxide);
  }
  .otherflag a {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
</style>
